  "interpretation": "For a smooth (step) source the integrator matches the closed-form solution to ~5e-7 pointwise. For the on/off source the pointwise maximum is larger (~7e-3) and occurs AT the switch instants only: the integrator interpolates the source linearly between grid points whereas the reference switches instantaneously, so the two differ over one grid interval at each edge. That is a difference in how a discontinuous forcing is represented, not accumulated integration error, which is why the area under the curve -- the reported quantity -- agrees to ~8e-5. No reported result is a pointwise value at a switch instant."
